<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    strings.xml — CENTRALIZED TEXT CONTENT

    WHY THIS EXISTS:
    All user-visible text belongs here, NOT hardcoded in Java or XML layouts.
    Benefits:
    1. Easy to change text in one place — e.g., rename "SOS" to "Emergency Alert"
       and it updates everywhere.
    2. Required for Localization (if you ever want Hindi/Tamil support,
       you just create a strings.xml in the right folder).
    3. Android Lint warns you if you hardcode a string directly in XML.
-->
